      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The \"soft\" weight limit refers to the fact that Eurostar staff have some discretion when it comes to checking luggage that's close to the weight limit. It's not a hard and fast rule, but rather a guideline. If your luggage is within 1-2kg of the weight limit, they might not be too keen on letting you on board, but they might make an exception if you're a frequent traveler or have a good reason for carrying extra luggage. It's a bit like a goblin's word - they might not always keep their promises, but they'll try to be reasonable.\n\nAs for the last part, I was just saying that you should check the Eurostar's website for any specific luggage restrictions or requirements, like a goblin checking for hidden traps in a dark cave. But don't worry, I won't bore you with more goblin analogies.\n\nTo answer your original question, the Eurostar's checked luggage weight limit is 23kg (50lbs), and the carry-on luggage weight limit is 10kg (22lbs). You can check-in online up to 30 days before your journey, and you'll need to arrive at least 30 minutes before your train departs.",
